This was played on nethack.alt.org, finished Sep 30 about 5:30 am :-)

After losing two wizards (one wishless, carrying Izchak, on Astral
[fishpool.fi]; the other with marked VS, waiting for Orcus to summon
Demo, messed up with a rubber chicken [alt.org]), I decided that this
ain't going to be the third class I ascend.

So I considered Valkyries, for a change, and thought about an
interesting conduct...

Trehe was alctauly nohitng worng wtih gimlz the Vyaklrie. She jsut had
some prbloems in shoocl: spelnlig, rdeinag and such wrer not her tihng.
[in theme with current UL about new university "research" :)]

So she thought she will show all her bumptious scroll-reading,
spell-casting, E-word-engraving sisters at the Shrine of Destiny and
would be the one who retrieved the Amulet of Yendor, shrouded in legend!

It proved not an easy task, however. She didn't find any bag long after
Sokoban and the Mines. Thrones she found extremely uncooperative, one
stole all her money, another wanted to genocide a whole race for her,
but as she didn't (or couldn't) pay much attention in school when they
discussed the folk and the beasts, so she only came up with 'none'.

Never got a single identify from those thrones. The wand of identify
rings [enlightenment] came only during the ascension run. Not even a
touchstone turned up to help her identify all those gems!

Not that she had good equipment to identify. She didn't find a means of
crossing water until after the castle. (The Orb helped reaching that
point.) She did find a +4 orcish helm and a +2 elven cloak though, which
she didn't wear, but stashed for later. In the Planes, every point of AC
was going to matter.

The break came a bit earlier though, when a water demon appeared while
she was diluting some potions. She wished for a gray dragon scale mail
and got it +0. Of course, when there are no means for further
enchantment.

At the quest, after retrieving the Orb of Weight, she finally rubbed her
(only) magic lamp and wished for a bag of holding, for she really needed
it by that time.

=oS proved not good enough for those damn traps causing irreparable
damage, so she was wielding Excalibur quite a lot. When she got crowned,
which was deliberate, she expected it's +1 enchantment to be raised, but
that's not how it works, she found out. It would have been wiser to
wield Mjollnir...

When she saw that there were no means for crossing water, she decided to
do Ludios to see what's to be found there. She only got the money and
took along about 6 pages of armor to buc-identify at an altar. And there
was nothing really good among the lot. She kept her old +4 helm and +2
elven cloak for the ascension, but now also had a cloak of protection
for the mid-game, which had the same AC as the elven one (but was more
vulnerable).

The money was useful enough, a priest lowered her naked AC from 1 to -1.

At the castle, a master mind flayer finally managed to get hold of her
the cotton in her head and sucked some of her anywise poor knowledge.
She went back to Dlvl 1 to remap the way.

The wand of wishing (of course) turned out to be 0:1, so 2 wishes was
all she was going to get. glimz decided for speed boots, but being an
ignorant illiterate, forgot to wish them up as fireproofed. (Of course)
they were +0..

She went down, her biggest fear--dying of boredom in Gehennom,
especially while looking for Vlad's. [YANI: there should be some tricky
way of obtaining the knowledge of it's whereabouts, relative to the
demon's lairs in the current game, perhaps (Oracle, quest leader?)!].

Vlad's staircase was very near the entrance to (I think it was) Asmo
though, and thus quickly found. She even got a wish from his throne! Now
I will use the wishing spoiler I thought--copy & paste. I will get
speedboots, fireproof, and this time they GOT to be +2.

Great idea, but I noticed an error in the spoiler--"rustproof speed
boots" it said, "fireproof" it should have been (at least in the
versions I know of). So I quickly ssh'd to correct that, but in the game
it was already pasted. Now, I know it would have worked anyway, but it
just didn't seem right..

So I, as I had just done it in vi... pressed the LEFT ARROW BUTTON.
ARGH! Damn terminals! I didn't get any speed boots. I got a blue,
worthless peace of GLASS! Wait, I'll take that back. I didn't even get
it--it fell to the ground as I was full of stuff hoping for a throne
identify. Talk about humiliation! [Anyway, this ridiculously expensive,
worthless peace of blue glass is to be admired in the inventory listing
below. (I may offer it at an auction at the demi-bar for most stupid
thing brought along..)]

I won't bore you with the details of Gehennom--it all went fine
obviously. During the run, the wizard was quite quiet. Found a wand of
enlightenment and, back at my stash, identified some rings which I
gulped as a xorn (had lost polyselfless due to a trap early on). On
Dlvl1, I wrestled that last charge out of the wand of wishing and
finally got those blessed fireproof +2 speed boots.

The elemental Planes were remarkably easy, perhaps because of the Orb.
On all but earth, glimz used it to find the portal. Here I should
mention that, even though she didn't plan to cast spells, she did
everything to raise her Int and, of course, also blessed and drank all
potions of gain ability and gain energy she found (the latter because
she was able to teleport).

On Astral, a gremlin appeared and I felt sickly, and the next creature
was a green dragon. That arranged a nice adrenaline rush: it was either
me or it. I managed to kill it and promptly ate the corpse to obtain
poison resistance again--whew!

I had an open account with Famine, so I chose that altar. This time it
didn't work out for Famine..

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...--More--










